Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:59:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1400/1463] HERESY 1447: LoRAs that run with the graph: a wave
 through the song, a budget shared
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor 14.10.2026: «LoRA ересь и алхимия»; 15.10.2026: «И не забудь за динамичную волну, именно ту, что ты воплотил в слайдерах стилей».

An adapter with a wave (the sliders' own, HERESY 1166) or in a budget is no longer merged at load: y = W x + g B (A x), A and B in F32 on the model's backend, g set before each step from its strength x its wave x its budget's share. The music half moves g at every frame it writes; the sound half takes a row of gains, one a frame of the chunk. A budget: the strengths of a group add up to its cap at most, shared in proportion or served in the request's order (what one adapter's wave lets go, the next one takes). An adapter's full deltas (realaudio's llm2vae and the like) stay merged at their flat strength while its A and B ride the wave. Flat adapters outside any budget are merged as before.

The request: a lora's "curve" (points or flat, arch, rise, fall) and "group"; "lora_groups": [{cap, mode: share|order}]; both written back with the take. The decode graph is keyed by the set's build, a model never keeps a set of a run before past its next require.

Measured on GPU2 (BF16): merged and on the graph agree token for token over all 600 frames at 0.75 (greedy), over 89 at 0.8 (a near tie; 0.75 against 0.8 merged part at 18); the sound half's latents 0.54 % apart (41 % from none). The set loads in under a second where a merge takes 9.6 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
